<div class="halacha-title">Hilchos Nedarim 2</div>
<!-- ══════════════════════════════ Section 1 ══════════════════════════════ -->
<span class="section-num">1.</span>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">עִנְיַן נְדָרִים וּשְׁבוּעוֹת שֶׁהֵם לִכְאוֹרָה דְּבַר תֵּמַהּ שֶׁיּוּכַל הָאָדָם לֶאֱסֹר עַל עַצְמוֹ אֵיזֶה דָּבָר אוֹ לְחַיֵּב עַצְמוֹ בְּדָבָר עַל-יְדֵי נֶדֶר וּשְׁבוּעָה. נִמְצָא, שֶׁהָאָדָם יָכוֹל לַעֲשׂוֹת לְעַצְמוֹ תּוֹרָה וּמִצְוֹת חֲדָשִׁים שֶׁאֵינָם מְפֹרָשִׁים בַּתּוֹרָה, כִּי עַל-יְדֵי נֶדֶר וּשְׁבוּעָה הוּא יָכוֹל לַעֲשׂוֹת לְעַצְמוֹ מִצְוָה וַעֲבֵרָה מִכָּל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם אַף-עַל-פִּי שֶׁאֵין בְּזֶה הַדָּבָר שׁוּם מִצְוָה וַעֲבֵרָה עַל-פִּי הַתּוֹרָה: אַךְ הָעִנְיָן עַל-פִּי מַה שֶּׁבֵּאֵר רַבֵּנוּ זַ״ל עַל פָּסוּק וָאֶתְחַנַּן אֶל ה' בָּעֵת הַהִוא לֵאמֹר בַּמַּאֲמָר הַמַּתְחִיל בְּעִנְיַן הַנְהָגַת הַפְּשִׁיטוּת שֶׁל הַצַּדִּיק הָאֱמֶת, עַיֵּן שָׁם הֵיטֵב (בְּלִקּוּטֵי תִּנְיָנָא סִימָן עח):</div>

<p class="first">The concept of <span class="key-term">nedarim</span> <span class="added">[vows]</span> and <span class="key-term">shevuos</span> <span class="added">[oaths]</span> — which are seemingly a matter of wonder — that a person can forbid upon himself some thing, or obligate himself in a matter, through a vow or an oath. It turns out that a person can create for himself new Torah <span class="added">[laws]</span> and <em>mitzvos</em> that are not specified in the Torah, for through a vow and an oath he can create for himself a <em>mitzvah</em> <span class="added">[commandment]</span> and an <em>avayrah</em> <span class="added">[transgression]</span> from any thing in the world, even though that thing carries no <em>mitzvah</em> or <em>avayrah</em> according to the Torah.</p>

<p>However, the explanation is based on what our Rebbe of blessed memory elucidated on the verse <span class="verse-inline">"And I beseeched Hashem at that time, saying"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Deuteronomy 3:23)</span>, in the discourse that begins with the topic of the conduct of <em>peshitus</em> <span class="added">[simplicity]</span> of the true <em>tzadik</em> — see there well (<span class="added">in</span> Likutay Moharan II, Torah 78).</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְתֹכֶן הַדָּבָר שָׁם שֶׁבְּעֵת שֶׁהַצַּדִּיק מִתְנַהֵג בְּדַרְכֵי הַפְּשִׁיטוּת כְּמוֹ אִישׁ פָּשׁוּט וְאֵינוֹ עוֹסֵק בַּתּוֹרָה אֲזַי הוּא מְחַיֶּה עַצְמוֹ בִּבְחִינַת קִיּוּם הָעוֹלָם קֹדֶם מַתַּן תּוֹרָה שֶׁאָז הָיָה מִתְקַיֵּם הָעוֹלָם בְּחַסְדּוֹ עַל-יְדֵי חֶסֶד חִנָּם מֵאַחַר שֶׁלֹּא הָיָה אָז שׁוּם הִתְגַּלּוּת הַתּוֹרָה בָּעוֹלָם. וּבֶאֱמֶת גַּם אָז הָיְתָה הַתּוֹרָה בָּעוֹלָם רַק שֶׁהָיְתָה בְּהֶעְלֵם, כִּי עֲשֶׂרֶת הַדִּבְּרוֹת הָיוּ נֶעְלָמִים בַּעֲשָׂרָה מַאֲמָרוֹת שֶׁבָּהֶם נִבְרָא הָעוֹלָם וְהָעֲשָׂרָה מַאֲמָרוֹת הֵם מְלֻבָּשִׁין בְּכָל דָּבָר וְדָבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם, כִּי הַכֹּל נִבְרָא בַּעֲשָׂרָה מַאֲמָרוֹת וְשָׁם נֶעְלָם הַתּוֹרָה בְּחִינַת עֲשֶׂרֶת הַדִּבְּרוֹת כַּנַּ״ל.</div>

<p>And the substance of the matter there is: that when the <em>tzadik</em> conducts himself in ways of <em>peshitus</em> <span class="added">[simplicity]</span>, like a simple person, and is not engaged in Torah — then he sustains himself through the aspect of the sustenance of the world before the giving of the Torah, when the world was sustained through His kindness, through <span class="key-term">chesed chinam</span> <span class="added">[gratuitous kindness]</span>, since at that time there was no revelation of the Torah in the world. And in truth, even then the Torah was in the world, only it was in a state of concealment. For the <span class="key-term">Aseres HaDibros</span> <span class="added">[Ten Commandments]</span> were concealed within the <span class="key-term">Asarah Ma'amaros</span> <span class="added">[Ten Utterances]</span> through which the world was created. And the Ten Utterances are clothed within each and every thing in the world, for everything was created through the Ten Utterances — and there the Torah is concealed, in the aspect of the Ten Commandments, as mentioned above.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְהַצַּדִּיק בְּעֵת פְּשִׁיטוּתוֹ, דְּהַיְנוּ בָּעֵת שֶׁמִּתְבַּטֵּל מִן הַתּוֹרָה הוּא מְחַיֶּה עַצְמוֹ בִּבְחִינָה זוֹ, בִּבְחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת בְּכָל מַעֲשֵׂה בְּרֵאשִׁית בְּכָל דָּבָר וְדָבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם, כִּי הַכֹּל נִבְרָא בַּעֲשָׂרָה מַאֲמָרוֹת וְכוּ' כַּנַּ״ל.</div>

<p>And the <em>tzadik</em> in the time of his simplicity — that is, at the time when he ceases from the Torah — sustains himself through this aspect: through the aspect of the Torah that is concealed in all the works of creation, in each and every thing in the world, for everything was created through the Ten Utterances, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה בְּחִינַת הַדֶּרֶךְ לְאֶרֶץ יִשְׂרָאֵל, כִּי עַל-יְדֵי בְּחִינַת הָעֲשָׂרָה מַאֲמָרוֹת, שֶׁהֵם בְּחִינַת כֹּחַ מַעֲשָׂיו, עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה יְכוֹלִין לִכְבֹּשׁ אֶרֶץ יִשְׂרָאֵל, כִּי בִּשְׁבִיל זֶה פָּתַח הַתּוֹרָה בִּבְרֵאשִׁית כְּדֵי שֶׁלֹּא יֹאמְרוּ לִסְטִים אַתֶּם וְכוּ', בִּשְׁבִיל זֶה פָּתַח בִּבְרֵאשִׁית, כִּי בִּרְצוֹנוֹ נְתָנָהּ לָהֶם וּבִרְצוֹנוֹ וְכוּ', עַיֵּן שָׁם הֵיטֵב כָּל הָעִנְיָן:</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <strong>path to Eretz Yisra'ail</strong>. For through the aspect of the Ten Utterances, which are the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">"the power of His works"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Psalms 111:6)</span> — through this one can conquer Eretz Yisra'ail. For it is for this reason that the Torah opened with <span class="verse-inline">"Beraishis"</span> <span class="added">[i.e. with the account of creation]</span> — so that the nations should not say, "You are robbers," etc. For this reason it opened with <em>Beraishis</em>: because by His will He gave it to them, and by His will, etc. <span class="added">[He took it from them and gave it to us]</span> — see there well, the entire matter.</p>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════ Section 2 ══════════════════════════════ -->
<span class="section-num">2.</span>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה בְּחִינַת נְדָרִים וּשְׁבוּעוֹת שֶׁהָאָדָם יָכוֹל לֶאֱסֹר עַל עַצְמוֹ כָּל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם וְלַעֲשׂוֹת מִכָּל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם תּוֹרָה, דְּהַיְנוּ שֶׁיִּהְיֶה בּוֹ מִצְוָה וַעֲבֵרָה עַל-יְדֵי נֶדֶר וּשְׁבוּעָה, כִּי בֶּאֱמֶת כָּל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם כֻּלָּם מְקַבְּלִים חִיּוּת עַל-יְדֵי הַתּוֹרָה, כִּי בִּלְעֲדֵי הַתּוֹרָה אֵין שׁוּם חִיּוּת לְשׁוּם דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם, כִּי אוֹרָיְתָא וְקֻדְשָׁא בְּרִיךְ הוּא כֹּלָּא חַד. וּבְוַדַּאי אֵין חִיּוּת לְשׁוּם דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם כִּי אִם מִמֶּנּוּ יִתְבָּרַךְ וְהוּא יִתְבָּרַךְ וְאוֹרָיְתָא כֹּלָּא חַד. כַּנַּ״ל, וּמֵחֲמַת זֶה יְכוֹלִין לַעֲבֹד אֶת ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ בְּכָל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, בְּכָל דְּרָכֶיךָ דָּעֵהוּ, כִּי בְּכֻלָּם מְלֻבָּשׁ הַתּוֹרָה כִּבְיָכוֹל, וְעַל-כֵּן יְכוֹלִין לְקַשֵּׁר הַכֹּל אֶל הַתּוֹרָה וְלַעֲשׂוֹת מִכָּל דָּבָר תּוֹרָה.</div>

<p class="first">And this is the aspect of <em>nedarim</em> and <em>shevuos</em> — that a person can forbid upon himself any thing in the world, and make Torah from any thing in the world — that is, that there should be in it a <em>mitzvah</em> and an <em>avayrah</em> through a vow and an oath. For in truth, all things in the world receive their <span class="key-term">chiyus</span> <span class="added">[life-force]</span> through the Torah. For without the Torah there is no life-force for anything in the world, for <span class="verse-inline">"Oraysa v'Kudsha Berich Hu kola chad"</span> <span class="added">[the Torah and the Holy One, blessed be He, are entirely one]</span>. And certainly there is no life-force for anything in the world except from Him, blessed be He — and He, blessed be He, and the Torah are entirely one, as mentioned above. And because of this, one can serve Hashem through all things in the world, as it is written: <span class="verse-inline">"In all your ways know Him"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Proverbs 3:6)</span>. For the Torah is clothed, as it were, in all of them. And therefore one can connect everything to the Torah and make Torah from every thing.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה גִּלְּתָה לָנוּ הַתּוֹרָה הַקְּדוֹשָׁה בְּמִצְוָה זוֹ שֶׁל נְדָרִים וּשְׁבוּעוֹת. שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי מִצְוָה זוֹ יְכוֹלִין לַעֲשׂוֹת תּוֹרָה וּמִצְוֹת מִכָּל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם כַּנַּ״ל. וּבָזֶה גִּלָּה לָנוּ ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ שֶׁיֵּשׁ תּוֹרָה וַעֲבוֹדָה בְּכָל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם, כִּי כֻּלָּם מְקַבְּלִין חִיּוּת מֵהַתּוֹרָה כַּנַּ״ל.</div>

<p>And this is what the holy Torah revealed to us through this <em>mitzvah</em> of <em>nedarim</em> and <em>shevuos</em> — that through this <em>mitzvah</em> one can make Torah and <em>mitzvos</em> from all things in the world, as mentioned above. And through this, Hashem revealed to us that there is Torah and <em>avodah</em> <span class="added">[divine service]</span> in every thing in the world, for they all receive their life-force from the Torah, as mentioned above.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה בְּחִינַת נְדָרִים וּשְׁבוּעוֹת, כִּי הַחִיּוּת אֱלֹקוּת הַמְלֻבָּשׁ בְּכָל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה יֵשׁ בָּזֶה שְׁנֵי בְּחִינוֹת, דְּהַיְנוּ בְּחִינַת קִיּוּם הָעוֹלָם קֹדֶם מַתַּן תּוֹרָה. וְכֵן עַכְשָׁו בְּעֵת שֶׁמִּתְבַּטְּלִין מִדִּבְרֵי תּוֹרָה בִּבְחִינַת בִּטּוּלָהּ שֶׁל תּוֹרָה זֶהוּ קִיּוּמָהּ, כִּי אָז מִתְקַיֵּם הָעוֹלָם עַל-יְדֵי חֶסֶד חִנָּם שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת הַעֲלָמַת הַתּוֹרָה שֶׁהַתּוֹרָה נֶעְלֶמֶת בַּעֲשָׂרָה מַאֲמָרוֹת וְכַנַּ״ל.</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of <em>nedarim</em> and <em>shevuos</em>. For the divine life-force that is clothed in all things of the world — which is the aspect of the Torah — has in it <strong>two aspects</strong>. That is, the aspect of the sustenance of the world before the giving of the Torah. And likewise now, at the time when one ceases from words of Torah — in the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">"the nullification of Torah, this is its sustenance"</span> — for then the world is sustained through gratuitous kindness, which is the aspect of the concealment of the Torah, that the Torah is concealed within the Ten Utterances, as mentioned above.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וּבְחִינָה זוֹ הִיא בְּחִינָה גָּבֹהַּ מְאֹד, כִּי הִיא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת בְּחִינַת סִתְרֵי תּוֹרָה שֶׁזֶּה בְּחִינַת חֶסֶד חִנָּם, בְּחִינַת אוֹצַר מַתְּנַת חִנָּם, שֶׁהִיא בְּחִינָה גָּבֹהַּ מְאֹד. כִּי בְּעֵת שֶׁאֵין הַתּוֹרָה בָּעוֹלָם אֲזַי אִי אֶפְשָׁר לְהָעוֹלָם לְהִתְקַיֵּם עַל-יְדֵי חֶסֶד סְתָם, כִּי אֵין הָעוֹלָם כְּדַאי לְהִתְקַיֵּם עַל-יְדֵי חֶסֶד פָּשׁוּט מֵאַחַר שֶׁאֵין תּוֹרָה בָּעוֹלָם עַל-כֵּן אֲזַי כְּשֶׁאֵין תּוֹרָה אֲזַי קִיּוּם הַתּוֹרָה עַל-יְדֵי בְּחִינַת חֶסֶד חִנָּם שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת שֶׁהִוא בְּחִינָה גָּבֹהַּ מְאֹד שֶׁמִּגֹּדֶל אוֹר הַחֶסֶד הַזֶּה שֶׁהוּא חֶסֶד חִנָּם, חֶסֶד גָּדוֹל מְאֹד יָכוֹל לְהִתְקַיֵּם הָעוֹלָם אַף-עַל-פִּי שֶׁאֵין הִתְגַּלּוּת הַתּוֹרָה בָּעוֹלָם.</div>

<p>And this aspect is a very lofty aspect, for it is the aspect of the concealed Torah, the aspect of <span class="key-term">sisray Torah</span> <span class="added">[the secrets of the Torah]</span> — and this is the aspect of <em>chesed chinam</em>, the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">"a storehouse of gratuitous gift"</span>, which is a very lofty aspect. For at the time when the Torah is not in the world, then it is impossible for the world to be sustained through ordinary <em>chesed</em>, for the world is not worthy of being sustained through simple kindness since there is no Torah in the world. Therefore, when there is no Torah, then the sustenance of the world is through the aspect of <em>chesed chinam</em>, which is the aspect of the concealed Torah, which is a very lofty aspect — for from the greatness of the light of this kindness, which is gratuitous kindness, an exceedingly great kindness, the world can be sustained even though there is no revelation of the Torah in the world.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">אֲבָל בֶּאֱמֶת אַף-עַל-פִּי שֶׁבְּחִינָה זוֹ גָּבֹהַּ מְאֹד אֵין זֶה שְׁלֵמוּת קִיּוּם הַתּוֹרָה, כִּי עִקַּר קִיּוּם הָעוֹלָם בִּשְׁלֵמוּת הוּא רַק עַל-יְדֵי קַבָּלַת הַתּוֹרָה שֶׁקִּבְּלוּ יִשְׂרָאֵל, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי וְכוּ'. וּפֵרֵשׁ רַשִׁ״י שֶׁכָּל הָעוֹלָם הָיָה תָּלוּי עַד שִׁשָּׁה בְּסִיוָן שֶׁקִּבְּלוּ יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת הַתּוֹרָה כִּי אֵין קִיּוּם לָעוֹלָם בְּלֹא הַתּוֹרָה, כִּי זֶה הַחִיּוּת וְהָאוֹר הַגָּדוֹל בְּחִינַת חֶסֶד חִנָּם שֶׁהָיָה מְקַיֵּם אֶת הָעוֹלָם קֹדֶם מַתַּן תּוֹרָה הוּא נֶעְלָם מְאֹד וּמִגֹּדֶל הֶעְלֵמוֹ, כִּי אֵינוֹ יָכוֹל לְהִתְלַבֵּשׁ כְּלָל בְּתוֹךְ הָעוֹלָם הוּא יָכוֹל לְהִתְעַלֵּם וּלְהִסְתַּלֵּק לְגַמְרֵי חַס וְשָׁלוֹם מֵהַעוֹלָם, וְיַחֲזֹר הָעוֹלָם לְתֹהוּ וָבֹהוּ חַס וְשָׁלוֹם.</div>

<p>But in truth, even though this aspect is very lofty, this is not the complete sustenance of the world. For the primary sustenance of the world in its completeness is only through the acceptance of the Torah that Israel accepted, as it is written, <span class="verse-inline">"<strong>The</strong> sixth day"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Genesis 1:31)</span> — <span class="added">[with a definitive "<em>hei</em>"]</span> and Rashi explained that the entire world was suspended until the sixth of Sivan when Israel accepted the Torah. For there is no sustenance for the world without the Torah. For this life-force and great light, the aspect of <em>chesed chinam</em> that was sustaining the world before the giving of the Torah — it is very concealed, and from the greatness of its concealment, since it cannot clothe itself at all within the world, it could become entirely concealed and depart, G-d forbid, from the world — and the world would return to <span class="verse-inline">"chaos and void"</span>, G-d forbid.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">עַל-כֵּן צָפָה ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ שֶׁאֵין הָעוֹלָם מִתְקַיֵּם בְּלֹא תּוֹרָה, עַל-כֵּן נָתַן הַתּוֹרָה תֵּכֶף אַחַר עֶשְׂרִים וְשִׁשָּׁה דּוֹרוֹת, כְּמוֹ שֶׁדָּרְשׁוּ רַבּוֹתֵינוּ זַ״ל עַל פָּסוּק דָּבָר צִוָּה לְאֶלֶף דּוֹר. כִּי עִקַּר קִיּוּם הָעוֹלָם הוּא עַל-יְדֵי הַתּוֹרָה שֶׁהִלְבִּישׁ, כִּבְיָכוֹל, ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ אֶת הָאוֹר הַנֶּעְלָם וְהַגָּנוּז בְּתוֹךְ אוֹתִיּוֹת הַתּוֹרָה הַקְּדוֹשָׁה. וְעַל-יְדֵי שֶׁיִּשְׂרָאֵל מְקַיְּמִין אֶת הַתּוֹרָה וְעוֹסְקִים בָּהּ, עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה הֵם מַמְשִׁיכִים אֱלֹקוּתוֹ יִתְבָּרַךְ בְּתוֹךְ הָעוֹלָם עַל-יְדֵי צִמְצוּמִים שֶׁל אוֹתִיּוֹת הַתּוֹרָה וְעַל-כֵּן עַל-יְדֵי הַתּוֹרָה נִתְבַּסֵּס הָעוֹלָם, כִּי עַל-יְדֵי הַתּוֹרָה הַקְּדוֹשָׁה מַמְשִׁיכִין הַחִיּוּת לְכָל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם, כִּי בְּלֹא הַתּוֹרָה חַס וְשָׁלוֹם, הָיָה אוֹר הַגָּנוּז מִסְתַּלֵּק מִגֹּדֶל הֶעְלֵמוֹ.</div>

<p>Therefore Hashem foresaw that the world cannot be sustained without the Torah. Therefore He gave the Torah immediately after twenty-six generations, as our Sages of blessed memory expounded on the verse <span class="verse-inline">"He commanded a word for a thousand generations"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Psalms 105:8)</span>. For the primary sustenance of the world is through the Torah, through which Hashem clothed, as it were, the concealed and hidden light within the letters of the holy Torah. And through Israel fulfilling the Torah and engaging in it, through this they draw His G-dliness, blessed be He, into the world — through the <span class="key-term">tzimtzumim</span> <span class="added">[contractions]</span> of the letters of the Torah. And therefore through the Torah the world is established, for through the holy Torah the life-force is drawn to all things in the world — for without the Torah, G-d forbid, the hidden light would depart from the greatness of its concealment.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">רַק אַף-עַל-פִּי-כֵן גַּם עַכְשָׁו בְּעֵת שֶׁמֻּכְרָחִין לְבַטֵּל מִדִּבְרֵי תּוֹרָה, כִּי אִי אֶפְשָׁר לַעֲסֹק בַּתּוֹרָה יוֹם וָלַיְלָה בְּלִי הֶפְסֵק רֶגַע. וּכְמוֹ שֶׁבֵּאֵר רַבֵּנוּ זַ״ל בַּמַּאֲמָר הַנַּ״ל אֲזַי בְּעֵת בִּטּוּל תּוֹרָה הַצַּדִּיק מְחַיֶּה עַצְמוֹ בִּבְחִינַת קִיּוּם הָעוֹלָם קֹדֶם מַתַּן תּוֹרָה שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת חֶסֶד חִנָּם שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת בַּעֲשָׂרָה מַאֲמָרוֹת וְכוּ', כַּמְבֹאָר שָׁם, עַיֵּן שָׁם.</div>

<p>Only, nevertheless, also now — at the time when one is compelled to cease from words of Torah, for it is impossible to engage in the Torah day and night without a moment's pause — and as our Rebbe of blessed memory explained in the aforementioned discourse — then, at the time of cessation from Torah, the <em>tzadik</em> sustains himself through the aspect of the sustenance of the world before the giving of the Torah, which is the aspect of <em>chesed chinam</em>, which is the aspect of the concealed Torah within the Ten Utterances, etc. — as is explained there; see there.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה בְּחִינַת נְדָרִים וּשְׁבוּעוֹת שֶׁהֵם שְׁתֵּי בְּחִינוֹת הַנַּ״ל. נֶדֶר זֶה בְּחִינַת הַחִיּוּת אֱלֹקוּת כִּבְיָכוֹל שֶׁהָיָה מְקַיֵּם הָעוֹלָם קֹדֶם מַתַּן תּוֹרָה שֶׁהִיא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת כַּנַּ״ל שֶׁמִּשָּׁם מְקַבְּלִין חִיּוּת כָּל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם בְּהֶעְלֵם גָּדוֹל.</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of <em>nedarim</em> and <em>shevuos</em>, which are the aforementioned two aspects. A <strong>neder</strong> <span class="added">[vow]</span> — this is the aspect of the divine life-force, as it were, that was sustaining the world before the giving of the Torah, which is the aspect of the concealed Torah, as mentioned above, from which all things in the world receive their life-force in a great state of concealment.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְעַל-כֵּן כְּשֶׁהָאָדָם נוֹדֵר אֵיזֶה נֶדֶר אֲזַי הוּא עוֹלֶה לִמְקוֹם הַנֶּדֶר שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת, שֶׁזֶּהוּ בְּחִינַת נֶדֶר שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת בִּינָה עָלְמָא דְּאִתְכַּסְּיָא, כַּמּוּבָא. וַאֲזַי מְקַשֵּׁר זֶה הַדָּבָר שֶׁהוּא נוֹדֵר עָלָיו בִּבְחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת בּוֹ, כִּי בְּכָל דָּבָר נֶעְלָם הַתּוֹרָה כַּנַּ״ל, הַיְנוּ שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי הַנֶּדֶר שֶׁמּוֹצִיא בְּפִיו עַל הַדָּבָר הַזֶּה, עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה הוּא מְגַלֶּה הַחִיּוּת אֱלֹקוּת הַנֶּעְלָם בְּזֶה הַדָּבָר שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינָה הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת, שֶׁזֶּהוּ בְּעַצְמוֹ בְּחִינַת נֶדֶר כַּנַּ״ל.</div>

<p>Therefore, when a person makes a vow, he ascends to the place of the <em>neder</em>, which is the aspect of the concealed Torah — and this is the aspect of a <em>neder</em>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Binah</span>, <span class="key-term">alma d'iskasya</span> <span class="added">[the concealed world]</span>, as is brought. And then he connects that thing upon which he is vowing to the aspect of the Torah concealed within it — for in every thing the Torah is concealed, as mentioned above. That is, through the vow that he utters with his mouth upon this thing, through this he reveals the divine life-force concealed in this thing, which is the aspect of the concealed Torah — and this itself is the aspect of a <em>neder</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וַאֲזַי כְּשֶׁעוֹשֶׂה נֶדֶר וּמְגַלֶּה שֶׁיֵּשׁ בְּזֶה הַדָּבָר הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת אֲזַי נַעֲשֶׂה מִזֶּה הַדָּבָר תּוֹרָה, כִּי בֶּאֱמֶת בְּכָל דָּבָר יֵשׁ תּוֹרָה רַק שֶׁהוּא בְּהֶעְלֵם וְהֶסְתֵּר גָּדוֹל, אֲבָל כְּשֶׁעוֹשֶׂה נֶדֶר בְּפִיו אֲזַי הוּא מְגַלֶּה הַעֲלָמָה זוֹ וַאֲזַי נַעֲשֶׂה מִזֶּה הַדָּבָר תּוֹרָה. וְעַל-כֵּן עִקַּר הַנֶּדֶר הוּא רַק כְּשֶׁמּוֹצִיאוֹ בְּפִיו וּדְבָרִים שֶׁבַּלֵּב אֵינָם דְּבָרִים, כִּי עִקַּר הַדָּבָר הוּא לְגַלּוֹת הַהַעֲלָמָה שֶׁזֶּהוּ בְּחִינַת תּוֹרָה, כְּמוֹ שֶׁאִיתָא בַּזֹּהַר הַקָּדוֹשׁ, מַאי תּוֹרָה דְּאוֹרֵי וְגָלֵי בַּמֶּה דַּהֲוֵי סְתִים.</div>

<p>And then, when he makes a vow and reveals that in this thing there is the concealed Torah, then this thing becomes Torah. For in truth, in every thing there is Torah, only it is in a great state of concealment and hiddenness. But when he makes a vow with his mouth, then he reveals this concealment, and then Torah is made from this thing. Therefore, a vow is primarily effective only when one utters it with his mouth, and <span class="verse-inline">"thoughts of the heart are not considered words"</span> — because the essence of the matter is to reveal the concealment, and this is the aspect of <strong>Torah</strong>. As it is found in the holy Zohar: <span class="verse-inline">"What is Torah? That which reveals and discloses what was hidden"</span> <span class="added">[<em>Mai Torah? D'oray v'galay b'mah d'havay sesim</em>]</span>.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה בְּחִינַת נֶדֶר שֶׁמּוֹצִיא בְּפִיו, כִּי עִקַּר הַהִתְגַּלּוּת הוּא בְּפִיו בִּבְחִינַת מִפִּיו דַּעַת וּתְבוּנָה. וְעַל-כֵּן כְּשֶׁמּוֹצִיא הַנֶּדֶר בְּפִיו הוּא מְגַלֶּה הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת שֶׁבְּזֶה הַדָּבָר שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינָה נֶדֶר כַּנַּ״ל עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁמּוֹצִיא הַנֶּדֶר בְּפִיו, שֶׁזֶּהוּ בְּחִינָה שֶׁמְּגַלֶּה מַה דַּהֲוֵי סְתִים וְעַל-כֵּן נַעֲשֶׂה מִזֶּה תּוֹרָה, כִּי זֶהוּ בְּחִינַת תּוֹרָה כַּנַּ״ל.</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of a <em>neder</em> that one utters with his mouth, for the primary revelation is through the mouth, in the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">"From His mouth, knowledge and understanding"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Proverbs 2:6)</span>. And therefore, when he utters the vow with his mouth, he reveals the concealed Torah within that thing — which is the aspect of a <em>neder</em>, as mentioned above — through uttering the vow with his mouth, which is the aspect of revealing what was hidden. And therefore Torah is made from this, for this is the aspect of Torah, as mentioned above.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה הַדָּבָר תָּלוּי בִּבְחִירַת הָאָדָם כְּפִי מַה שֶּׁרוֹצֶה לְגַלּוֹת אוֹר הַנֶּעְלָם הַזֶּה אִם לַעֲשׂוֹת אִם שֶׁלֹּא לַעֲשׂוֹת, כִּי זֶה הָאוֹר הַנֶּעְלָם הוּא בְּחִינַת אוֹר פָּשׁוּט שֶׁאֵין בּוֹ שׁוּם צִיּוּר שֶׁל מִצְוָה וַעֲבֵרָה רַק זֶה תָּלוּי בִּבְחִירַת הָאָדָם כְּפִי מַה שֶּׁמַּמְשִׁיךְ הָאוֹר לְמַטָּה אִם לַעֲשׂוֹת אִם לַחְדֹּל וַאֲזַי נַעֲשֶׂה מִזֶּה תּוֹרָה כְּפִי מַה שֶּׁהוּא מַמְשִׁיךְ הָאוֹר מֵהַהֶעְלֵם אֶל הַגִּלּוּי, דְּהַיְנוּ כְּפִי מַה שֶּׁנּוֹדֵר בְּפִיו שֶׁזֶּה בְּחִינַת שֶׁמְּגַלֶּה מַה דַּהֲוֵי סָתוּם כַּנַּ״ל וְהָבֵן הֵיטֵב:</div>

<p>And this matter depends on the <strong>free choice</strong> of the person — according to how he wishes to reveal this concealed light, whether to do or not to do. For this concealed light is an aspect of <strong>simple light</strong> (<span class="key-term">or pashut</span>) in which there is no form whatsoever of <em>mitzvah</em> and <em>avayrah</em>. Rather, it depends on the free choice of the person — according to how he draws the light downward, whether to do or to refrain. And then Torah is made from this, according to how he draws the light from concealment to revelation — that is, according to what he vows with his mouth, which is the aspect of revealing what was sealed, as mentioned above. Understand this well.</p>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════ Section 3 ══════════════════════════════ -->
<span class="section-num">3.</span>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">נִמְצָא, שֶׁעִנְיַן נְדָרִים הוּא שֶׁמְּקַשֵּׁר הַדָּבָר לְהַחִיּוּת אֱלֹקוּת שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת שֶׁנֶּעְלָם בְּכָל דָּבָר, הַיְנוּ שֶׁמְּגַלֶּה מַה דַּהֲוֵי סְתִים שֶׁמְּגַלֶּה שֶׁגַּם שָׁם נֶעְלָם אוֹר גָּדוֹל בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת, וַאֲזַי נַעֲשֶׂה מִזֶּה הַדָּבָר בְּחִינַת תּוֹרָה, דְּהַיְנוּ שֶׁיֵּשׁ בּוֹ מִצְוָה וַעֲבֵרָה כִּי הוּא מְחֻיָּב לְקַיֵּם הַדָּבָר וְאָסוּר לוֹ לַעֲבֹר עַל הַדָּבָר שֶׁנָּדַר עָלָיו. נִמְצָא שֶׁנַּעֲשֶׂה תּוֹרָה וּמִצְוָה מִזֶּה הַדָּבָר, שֶׁמִּתְּחִלָּה לֹא הָיָה בּוֹ שׁוּם מִצְוָה וַעֲבֵרָה, כִּי עַכְשָׁו נַעֲשֶׂה מִזֶּה הַדָּבָר בְּחִינַת תּוֹרָה עַל-יְדֵי הַנֶּדֶר שֶׁהוֹצִיא בְּפִיו שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה מְגַלֶּה מַה דַּהֲוֵי סְתִים שֶׁמְּגַלֶּה הַעֲלָמַת הַתּוֹרָה שֶׁהָיְתָה נֶעְלֶמֶת שָׁם כַּנַּ״ל וְזֶה בְּחִינַת נֶדֶר שֶׁמְּגַלֶּה בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת קִיּוּם הָעוֹלָם בְּעֵת בִּטּוּל תּוֹרָה בְּעֵת הַנְהָגַת הַפְּשִׁיטוּת כַּנַּ״ל:</div>

<p class="first">It emerges that the concept of <em>nedarim</em> is that one connects the thing to the divine life-force, which is the aspect of the concealed Torah that is hidden in every thing. That is, he reveals what was hidden — he reveals that also there, a great light is concealed, the aspect of the concealed Torah. And then, this thing becomes an aspect of Torah — that is, there is in it a <em>mitzvah</em> and an <em>avayrah</em>, for he is obligated to fulfill the matter and it is forbidden for him to transgress that which he vowed upon. It turns out that Torah and <em>mitzvah</em> are made from this thing, which initially had no <em>mitzvah</em> or <em>avayrah</em> in it at all. For now this thing has become an aspect of Torah through the vow that he uttered with his mouth — through which he reveals what was hidden, revealing the concealment of the Torah that was concealed there, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of a <em>neder</em> — which reveals the aspect of the concealed Torah, which is the aspect of the sustenance of the world at the time of the cessation of Torah, at the time of the conduct of simplicity, as mentioned above.</p>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════ Section 4 ══════════════════════════════ -->
<span class="section-num">4.</span>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וּשְׁבוּעָה זֶהוּ הַבְּחִינָה הַשְּׁנִיָּה, הַיְנוּ כִּי בֶּאֱמֶת עִקַּר קִיּוּם הָעוֹלָם הוּא רַק עַל-יְדֵי הַתּוֹרָה שֶׁקִּבְּלוּ יִשְׂרָאֵל שֶׁעַל יָדָהּ נִמְשָׁךְ הַשֶּׁפַע וְהַחִיּוּת לְכָל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם וְכַנַּ״ל. וְזֶה בְּחִינַת שְׁבוּעָה, כִּי שְׁבוּעָה הִוא בְּחִינַת כְּלָלִיּוּת הַתּוֹרָה, שֶׁהִיא כְּלוּלָה מִשִּׁבְעַת יְמֵי הַבִּנְיָן, שֶׁזֶּה בְּחִינַת שְׁבוּעָה לְשׁוֹן שִׁבְעָה, כִּי בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת, בְּחִינַת נֶדֶר הִוא לְמַעְלָה מִשִּׁבְעַת יְמֵי הַבִּנְיָן כַּיָּדוּעַ. אֲבָל הַתּוֹרָה הַמְּסוּרָה בְּיָדֵינוּ הִוא בְּחִינַת שְׁבוּעָה, בְּחִינַת שִׁבְעָה כַּנַּ״ל.</div>

<p class="first">And a <strong>shevuah</strong> <span class="added">[oath]</span> — this is the <strong>second aspect</strong>. That is, in truth, the primary sustenance of the world is only through the Torah that Israel received, through which abundance and life-force is drawn to all things in the world, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of a <em>shevuah</em>. For a <em>shevuah</em> is the aspect of the totality of the Torah, which is comprised of the <span class="key-term">shivas yemai habinyan</span> <span class="added">[seven days of construction]</span>. And this is the aspect of <em>shevuah</em> — from the root <strong><em>sheva</em></strong> <span class="added">[seven]</span>. For the aspect of the concealed Torah — the aspect of a <em>neder</em> — is above the seven days of construction, as is known. But the Torah that was transmitted into our hands is the aspect of a <em>shevuah</em>, the aspect of seven, as mentioned above.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְעִקַּר קִיּוּם הָעוֹלָם בִּשְׁלֵמוּת הוּא רַק עַל-יְדֵי הַתּוֹרָה, דְּהַיְנוּ עַל-יְדֵי עֵסֶק הַתּוֹרָה וְהַמִּצְוֹת שֶׁעַל יָדָם נִמְשָׁךְ הַשֶּׁפַע וְהַחִיּוּת לְכָל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם וְעַל-כֵּן כְּשֶׁהָאָדָם אוֹמֵר לְשׁוֹן שְׁבוּעָה וְאוֹסֵר עַצְמוֹ עַל אֵיזֶה דָּבָר נַעֲשֶׂה מִזֶּה הַדָּבָר גַּם כֵּן תּוֹרָה, כִּי יֵשׁ בְּיָדוֹ זֶה הַכֹּחַ מֵאַחַר שֶׁהָאָדָם הוּא מַמְשִׁיךְ חִיּוּת הַתּוֹרָה לְכָל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם עַל-כֵּן יֵשׁ בְּיָדוֹ כֹּחַ לַעֲשׂוֹת מִכָּל הַדְּבָרִים תּוֹרָה, דְּהַיְנוּ שֶׁיֵּשׁ בְּיָדוֹ כֹּחַ לְהַמְשִׁיךְ הַחִיּוּת לְשָׁם כִּרְצוֹנוֹ אִם לְחִיּוּב שֶׁיִּהְיֶה מְחֻיָּב לַעֲשׂוֹתוֹ אִם לְהֵפֶךְ עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁמַּזְכִּיר לְשׁוֹן שְׁבוּעָה שֶׁהִוא בְּחִינַת כְּלָלִיּוּת הַתּוֹרָה שֶׁמִּשָּׁם כָּל הַדְּבָרִים מְקַבְּלִין הַחִיּוּת. וּכְשֶׁמַּזְכִּיר זֶה הַלָּשׁוֹן לֶאֱסֹר עַל עַצְמוֹ אֵיזֶה דָּבָר אוֹ לְחַיֵּב עַצְמוֹ בְּדָבָר הֲרֵי הוּא מַמְשִׁיךְ חִיּוּת הַתּוֹרָה לְשָׁם בִּבְחִינָה זוֹ, דְּהַיְנוּ שֶׁיִּהְיֶה נִמְשָׁךְ הַחִיּוּת שֶׁל הַתּוֹרָה לְאוֹתוֹ הַדָּבָר לְמִצְוָה אוֹ לְהֵפֶךְ, דְּהַיְנוּ לַעֲשׂוֹת אוֹ שֶׁלֹּא לַעֲשׂוֹת וַאֲזַי נַעֲשֶׂה מִזֶּה הַדָּבָר גַּם כֵּן תּוֹרָה וְיֵשׁ בּוֹ מִצְוָה וַעֲבֵרָה עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁהִמְשִׁיךְ חִיּוּת הַתּוֹרָה לְשָׁם בִּבְחִינָה זוֹ כְּפִי שְׁבוּעָתוֹ הֵן אוֹ לָאו:</div>

<p>And the primary sustenance of the world in its completeness is only through the Torah — that is, through the engagement in Torah and <em>mitzvos</em>, through which abundance and life-force is drawn to all things in the world. Therefore, when a person says the expression of a <em>shevuah</em> and forbids himself regarding some thing, that thing also becomes Torah. For he has this power, since man draws the life-force of the Torah to all things in the world — therefore he has the power to make Torah from all things. That is, he has the power to draw the life-force there as he wishes — whether as an obligation, that he shall be obligated to do it, or the opposite — through mentioning the expression of a <em>shevuah</em>, which is the aspect of the totality of the Torah, from which all things receive their life-force. And when he mentions this expression to forbid upon himself some thing, or to obligate himself in a matter, behold, he draws the life-force of the Torah there in this aspect — that is, the life-force of the Torah is drawn to that thing as a <em>mitzvah</em> or the reverse — that is, to do or not to do. And then this thing also becomes Torah, and there is in it <em>mitzvah</em> and <em>avayrah</em> — through his having drawn the life-force of the Torah there in this aspect, according to his oath, whether affirmative or negative.</p>
<!-- ══════════════════════════════ Section 5 ══════════════════════════════ -->
<span class="section-num">5.</span>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">נִמְצָא, שֶׁנְּדָרִים וּשְׁבוּעוֹת הֵם בְּחִינָה אַחַת, דְּהַיְנוּ שֶׁעוֹשֶׂה מִדְּבָרִים שֶׁל הָעוֹלָם תּוֹרָה, דְּהַיְנוּ מִצְוָה וַעֲבֵרָה עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁמְּקַשֵּׁר הַדָּבָר לְהַתּוֹרָה וּמְגַלֶּה שֶׁגַּם בָּהֶם יֵשׁ תּוֹרָה וְכֻלָּם מְקַבְּלִים חִיּוּת מֵהַתּוֹרָה כַּנַּ״ל רַק שֶׁהַנֶּדֶר הוּא שֶׁמְּגַלֶּה הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת בְּאוֹתוֹ הַדָּבָר שֶׁהוּא לְמַעְלָה מֵהַתּוֹרָה, וְעַל-כֵּן נְדָרִים חָלִים עַל דְּבַר מִצְוָה, כִּי הַנֶּדֶר הוּא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת שֶׁהִוא לְמַעְלָה מֵהַתּוֹרָה.</div>

<p class="first">It turns out that <em>nedarim</em> and <em>shevuos</em> are one <span class="added">[unified]</span> aspect — that is, that one makes Torah from worldly things — that is, <em>mitzvah</em> and <em>avayrah</em> — through connecting the thing to the Torah and revealing that also in them there is Torah, and they all receive life-force from the Torah, as mentioned above. Only, the <em>neder</em> is that which reveals the <strong>concealed Torah</strong> within that thing — which is <strong>above</strong> the Torah. And therefore <strong><em>nedarim</em> take effect even upon a matter of <em>mitzvah</em></strong>, for the <em>neder</em> is the aspect of the concealed Torah, which is above the Torah.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וּשְׁבוּעָה הִוא בְּחִינַת שֶׁעוֹשֶׂה מִזֶּה הַדָּבָר תּוֹרָה עַל-יְדֵי הַחִיּוּת וְהַשֶּׁפַע שֶׁהוּא מַמְשִׁיךְ לְהַדָּבָר מֵהַתּוֹרָה. וְעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה הוּא עוֹשֶׂה מֵאוֹתוֹ הַדָּבָר גַּם כֵּן תּוֹרָה. וְעַל-כֵּן אֵין שְׁבוּעָה חָלָה עַל דְּבַר מִצְוָה, כִּי עִקַּר כֹּחַ הַשְּׁבוּעָה הִוא מֵהַתּוֹרָה כַּנַּ״ל, אֲבָל נֶדֶר הוּא בְּחִינָה לְמַעְלָה מֵהַתּוֹרָה בְּחִינַת קִיּוּם הָעוֹלָם קֹדֶם מַתַּן תּוֹרָה, בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת כַּנַּ״ל.</div>

<p>And a <em>shevuah</em> is the aspect of making Torah from that thing through the life-force and abundance that one draws to the thing <em>from</em> the Torah. And through this, he makes from that thing also Torah. And therefore <strong>a <em>shevuah</em> does not take effect upon a matter of <em>mitzvah</em></strong>, for the primary power of the <em>shevuah</em> is from the Torah, as mentioned above. But a <em>neder</em> is an aspect that is above the Torah, the aspect of the sustenance of the world before the giving of the Torah, the aspect of the concealed Torah, as mentioned above.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה בְּחִינָה מַה שֶּׁאָמְרוּ רַבּוֹתֵינוּ זַ״ל נֶדֶר מִתְּסַר חֲפָצֵהּ עֲלֵהּ. שְׁבוּעָה מִתְּסַר נַפְשֵׁהּ אַחֲפָצֵהּ, כִּי הָאָדָם הוּא בְּעַצְמוֹ בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה, כְּמוֹ שֶׁאָמַר רַבֵּנוּ זַ״ל. וּכְמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, זֹאת הַתּוֹרָה אָדָם. (סִימָן יג) כִּי כָּל אָדָם כָּלוּל מִכָּל הַתּוֹרָה כֻּלָּהּ שֶׁהִוא רְמַ״ח מִצְוֹת עֲשֵׂה וּשְׁסָ״ה לֹא תַעֲשֶׂה שֶׁהֵם כְּנֶגֶד רְמַ״ח אֵיבָרִים וּשְׁסָ״ה גִּידִים שֶׁל הָאָדָם.</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of what our Sages of blessed memory said: <strong>"A <em>neder</em> — the object is forbidden upon him. A <em>shevuah</em> — he forbids himself upon the object"</strong> <span class="added">[<em>neder mitsar chaftzay alay; shevuah mitsar nafshay achaftzay</em>]</span>. For a person is himself the aspect of the Torah, as our Rebbe of blessed memory said. And as it is written, <span class="verse-inline">"This is the Torah: a man"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Numbers 19:14)</span> <span class="added">[see Likutay Moharan, Torah 13]</span>. For every person is comprised of the entire Torah — which is the 248 positive commandments and 365 negative commandments, corresponding to the 248 limbs and 365 sinews of a person.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְעַל-כֵּן כְּשֶׁעוֹשֶׂה שְׁבוּעָה שֶׁהִוא בְּחִינַת כְּלָלִיּוּת הַתּוֹרָה הוּא אוֹסֵר עַצְמוֹ עַל הַחֵפֶץ, הַיְנוּ שֶׁעִקַּר אִסּוּר הַשְּׁבוּעָה הוּא מֵחֲמַת שֶׁמַּמְשִׁיךְ הַחִיּוּת מֵהַתּוֹרָה אֶל הַדָּבָר בִּבְחִינָה זוֹ לַעֲשׂוֹת אוֹ שֶׁלֹּא לַעֲשׂוֹת. וְעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה נַעֲשֶׂה מִזֶּה תּוֹרָה וּמְחֻיָּב לְקַיֵּם כֵּן. וְעַל-כֵּן הוּא בְּחִינָה שֶׁאוֹסֵר עַצְמוֹ עַל הַחֵפֶץ, כִּי הוּא עַצְמוֹ הוּא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה וְהוּא מְחַיֶּה כָּל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁהוּא כָּלוּל מֵהַתּוֹרָה, כִּי הָאָדָם הוּא כְּלָלִיּוּת הָעוֹלָם וְכָל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם מְקַבְּלִין חִיּוּת מִמֶּנּוּ עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁהוּא כָּלוּל מֵהַתּוֹרָה. נִמְצָא, כְּשֶׁעוֹשֶׂה הַחֵפֶץ בִּבְחִינַת אִסּוּר שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה נַעֲשֶׂה מִזֶּה תּוֹרָה וְנֶאֱסָר עָלָיו כַּנַּ״ל.</div>

<p>Therefore, when one makes a <em>shevuah</em>, which is the aspect of the totality of the Torah, he forbids <strong>himself</strong> upon the object. That is, the primary prohibition of the <em>shevuah</em> is because he draws the life-force from the Torah to the thing in this manner — to do or not to do. And through this, Torah is made from it, and he is obligated to fulfill it accordingly. And therefore it is the aspect of forbidding himself upon the object — for he himself is the aspect of the Torah, and he sustains all things in the world through his being comprised of the Torah. For man is the totality of the world, and all things in the world receive life-force from him through his being comprised of the Torah. It turns out that when he makes the object into an aspect of prohibition, through this, Torah is made from it, and it becomes forbidden to him, as mentioned above.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">אֲבָל הַנֶּדֶר הוּא בְּחִינָה לְמַעְלָה מֵהַתּוֹרָה בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת וְשָׁם הוּא לְהֵפֶךְ בְּחִינַת הַמְשָׁכַת הַחִיּוּת מֵעֵלָּא לְתַתָּא בִּבְחִינַת תּוֹרָה הֵן אוֹ לָאו, הַיְנוּ שֶׁהוּא מַמְשִׁיךְ וּמְגַלֶּה הַחִיּוּת הַנֶּעְלָם בְּזֶה הַדָּבָר בִּבְחִינַת תּוֹרָה מֵעֵלָּא לְתַתָּא, כִּי זֶה הַחִיּוּת הַנֶּעְלָם הוּא גָּבֹהַּ מְאֹד. וְזֶה הַחִיּוּת הַנֶּעְלָם בְּחִינַת נֶדֶר הוּא מְקַיֵּם הָעוֹלָם בְּלִי הִתְעוֹרְרוּת תַּחְתּוֹן כְּלָל, כִּי זֶהוּ בְּחִינַת קִיּוּם הָעוֹלָם קֹדֶם קַבָּלַת הַתּוֹרָה. נִמְצָא, שֶׁאֵין זֶה הַחִיּוּת נִמְשָׁךְ עַל-יְדֵי הָאָדָם רַק ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ מְקַיֵּם הָעוֹלָם בְּעַצְמוֹ בְּחֶסֶד חִנָּם בְּלִי מַעֲשֵׂה הַתַּחְתּוֹנִים כְּלָל. וְעַל-כֵּן עַל-יְדֵי בְּחִינָה זוֹ הוּא יָכוֹל לַעֲשׂוֹת מִזֶּה הַדָּבָר בְּעַצְמוֹ תּוֹרָה וְלֶאֱסֹר הֶחָפֵץ בְּעַצְמוֹ עָלָיו, כִּי נַעֲשֶׂה מִמֶּנּוּ תּוֹרָה עַל-יְדֵי הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת שֶׁהִוא אֵינָהּ תְּלוּיָה בְּהָאָדָם כְּלָל כַּנַּ״ל, אֲבָל שְׁבוּעָה עִקָּרָהּ עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁהָאָדָם מְחַיֶּה הָעוֹלָמוֹת עַל-יְדֵי הַתּוֹרָה, עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה יָכוֹל לַעֲשׂוֹת תּוֹרָה מִכָּל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם, עַל-כֵּן הוּא בְּחִינַת מִתְּסַר נַפְשֵׁהּ אַחֲפָצֵהּ, כִּי הָאָדָם הוּא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה וְכַנַּ״ל:</div>

<p>But a <em>neder</em> is an aspect above the Torah, the aspect of the concealed Torah, and there it is the reverse — the aspect of drawing down the life-force <strong>from above to below</strong> in the aspect of Torah, whether affirmative or negative. That is, he draws and reveals the concealed life-force within this thing in the aspect of Torah, from above to below — for this concealed life-force is very lofty. And this concealed life-force, the aspect of a <em>neder</em>, sustains the world without any arousal from below whatsoever, for this is the aspect of the sustenance of the world before the acceptance of the Torah. It turns out that this life-force is not drawn through man; rather, Hashem sustains the world by Himself, through gratuitous kindness, without any action of the lower beings at all. And therefore, through this aspect, he can make Torah from this thing itself, and forbid <strong>the object itself</strong> upon himself — for Torah is made from it through the concealed Torah, which does not depend on man at all, as mentioned above. But a <em>shevuah</em> — its essence is that man sustains the worlds through the Torah; through this he can make Torah from all things in the world. Therefore it is the aspect of "he forbids himself upon the object" — for man is the aspect of the Torah, as mentioned above.</p>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════ Section 6 ══════════════════════════════ -->
<span class="section-num">6.</span>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְעַל-כֵּן בְּנֶדֶר אֵין שַׁיָּךְ בּוֹ שׁוּם שֵׁם וְכִנּוּי וְהַנּוֹדֵר בַּתּוֹרָה אֵינוֹ כְּלוּם, כִּי הַנֶּדֶר הוּא בְּחִינַת הַהַעֲלָמָה שֶׁשָּׁם נֶעְלָמִין כָּל הַשֵּׁמוֹת וְכָל הַתּוֹרָה הַקְּדוֹשָׁה הִוא בִּבְחִינַת הֶעְלֵם כַּנַּ״ל, אֲבָל הַשְּׁבוּעָה הִיא בְּשֵׁם וְכִנּוּי אוֹ נִשְׁבָּע בַּתּוֹרָה, כִּי שְׁבוּעָה הִוא בְּחִינַת כְּלָלִיּוּת הַתּוֹרָה שֶׁכְּלוּלָה מִשִּׁבְעָה כַּנַּ״ל שֶׁהִוא בְּחִינַת כְּלָלִיּוּת הַשֵּׁמוֹת שֶׁכְּלוּלִים בְּשִׁבְעָה שֵׁמוֹת שֶׁאֵינָם נִמְחָקִין וַאֲפִלּוּ כְּשֶׁנִּשְׁבַּע בְּלֹא שֵׁם וְכִנּוּי שֶׁגַּם כֵּן חָל אִסּוּר שְׁבוּעָה, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב בַּשֻּׁלְחָן עָרוּךְ. כִּי לְשׁוֹן שְׁבוּעָה בְּעַצְמוֹ הוּא בְּחִינָה זוֹ בְּחִינַת כְּלָלִיּוּת הַתּוֹרָה, בְּחִינַת כְּלָלִיּוּת הַשִּׁבְעָה שֵׁמוֹת שֶׁזֶּה בְּחִינַת לְשׁוֹן שְׁבוּעָה:</div>

<p class="first">Therefore, regarding a <em>neder</em>, no <span class="key-term">Shem</span> <span class="added">[Divine Name]</span> or <span class="key-term">kinui</span> <span class="added">[appellation]</span> is relevant to it, and one who vows "by the Torah" — it is nothing <span class="added">[i.e. the vow does not take effect]</span>. For the <em>neder</em> is the aspect of concealment, where all the Names are concealed, and the entire holy Torah is in a state of concealment, as mentioned above. But a <em>shevuah</em> is made with a Name and appellation, or one swears by the Torah. For a <em>shevuah</em> is the aspect of the totality of the Torah, which is comprised of seven, as mentioned above — which is the aspect of the totality of the Names, which are comprised of the <strong>seven Names that may not be erased</strong>. And even when one swears without a Name and appellation, the prohibition of the <em>shevuah</em> still takes effect, as is written in the <em>Shulchan Aruch</em>. For the expression of <em>shevuah</em> itself is this aspect — the aspect of the totality of the Torah, the aspect of the totality of the seven Names — and this is the aspect of the expression of <em>shevuah</em>.</p>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════ Section 7 ══════════════════════════════ -->
<span class="section-num">7.</span>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה שֶׁהִתְחִיל הַתַּנָּא מַסֶּכֶת נְדָרִים כָּל כִּנּוּיֵי נְדָרִים כִּנְדָרִים וְכוּ', כִּי נֶדֶר וּשְׁבוּעָה הוּא בְּחִינַת הַחִיּוּת אֱלֹקוּת כִּבְיָכוֹל, הַמִּתְפַּשֵּׁט בְּכָל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם וּבְכָל הַלְּשׁוֹנוֹת הַגּוֹיִים, שֶׁזֶּהוּ בְּחִינַת נֶדֶר וּשְׁבוּעָה שֶׁמְּגַלִּין שֶׁבְּכָל הַדְּבָרִים יֵשׁ אֱלֹקוּתוֹ יִתְבָּרַךְ כִּבְיָכוֹל וִיכוֹלִין לַעֲשׂוֹת מִכָּל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם תּוֹרָה וּמִצְוָה. וְעַל-כֵּן בַּנְּדָרִים הַלֵּךְ אַחַר לְשׁוֹן בְּנֵי אָדָם, כִּי בְּכָל הַלְּשׁוֹנוֹת יְכוֹלִין לַעֲשׂוֹת נֶדֶר, כִּי יְכוֹלִין לִמְצֹא אֱלֹקוּתוֹ בְּכָל הַדְּבָרִים וּבְכָל לְשׁוֹנוֹת הַגּוֹיִים, כִּי אֱלֹקוּתוֹ יִתְבָּרַךְ נֶעְלָם בְּכֻלָּם, כִּי מְחַיֶּה אֶת כֻּלָּם, שֶׁזֶּהוּ עִקַּר בְּחִינַת נֶדֶר וּשְׁבוּעָה וְכַנַּ״ל:</div>

<p class="first">And this is the reason the <em>Tanna</em> began Tractate Nedarim <span class="added">[with]</span>: <span class="verse-inline">"All <em>kinuyay</em> [substitutes for] <em>nedarim</em> are like <em>nedarim</em>"</span> etc. For a <em>neder</em> and <em>shevuah</em> are the aspect of the divine life-force, as it were, that spreads into all things in the world and into all the languages of the nations. And this is the aspect of a <em>neder</em> and <em>shevuah</em> — which reveal that in all things there is His G-dliness, blessed be He, as it were, and one can make Torah and <em>mitzvah</em> from every thing in the world. And therefore, <strong>regarding <em>nedarim</em>, we follow the language of people</strong> <span class="added">[<em>halach achar leshon bnay adam</em>]</span> — for in all languages one can make a vow, because one can find His G-dliness in all things and in all languages of the nations, for His G-dliness, blessed be He, is concealed in all of them, for He gives life to all of them — and this is the primary aspect of <em>neder</em> and <em>shevuah</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════ Section 8 ══════════════════════════════ -->
<span class="section-num">8.</span>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְעַל-כֵּן הֶחָכָם עוֹקֵר הַנֶּדֶר מֵעִקָּרוֹ, כִּי כָּל עִנְיַן נֶדֶר וּשְׁבוּעָה הוּא תָּלוּי בְּחָכָם וּגְדוֹל הַדּוֹר, כִּי עִנְיַן נֶדֶר וּשְׁבוּעָה הוּא שֶׁמְּגַלִּין שֶׁכָּל הַדְּבָרִים מְקַבְּלִין חִיּוּת מֵהַתּוֹרָה וְכוּ' כַּנַּ״ל. אֲבָל זֶה תָּלוּי רַק בְּהַגָּדוֹל וְהֶחָכָם שֶׁבַּדּוֹר. וּכְמוֹ שֶׁכָּתַב רַבֵּנוּ זַ״ל בַּמַּאֲמָר ״וָאֶתְחַנַּן״ הַנַּ״ל. שֶׁכָּל הַפְּשׁוּטִים צְרִיכִין אִישׁ פָּשׁוּט גָּדוֹל מְאֹד שֶׁעַל יָדוֹ כֻּלָּם מְקַבְּלִים חִיּוּת, עַיֵּן שָׁם הֵיטֵב.</div>

<p class="first">Therefore <strong>the <em>chacham</em> uproots the <em>neder</em> from its root</strong>. For the entire matter of <em>neder</em> and <em>shevuah</em> depends on the <em>chacham</em> <span class="added">[sage]</span> and the great one of the generation. For the concept of <em>neder</em> and <em>shevuah</em> is that one reveals that all things receive life-force from the Torah, etc., as mentioned above. But this depends only on the great one and the <em>chacham</em> of the generation. As our Rebbe of blessed memory wrote in the aforementioned discourse "<em>Va'eschanan</em>" — that all the simple people require a very great simple man, through whom they all receive life-force; see there well.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">כִּי בֶּאֱמֶת אִישׁ פָּשׁוּט הַקָּטָן בְּמַעֲלָה, דְּהַיְנוּ הֲמוֹן הָעָם בְּוַדַּאי אֵינָם מְחַיִּין אֶת הָעוֹלָם עַל-יְדֵי הַתּוֹרָה, כִּי אֵינָם בַּעֲלֵי תּוֹרָה וַאֲפִלּוּ מִי שֶׁעוֹסֵק בַּתּוֹרָה לָאו כָּל אֶחָד זוֹכֶה שֶׁהוּא יְקַיֵּם כָּל הָעוֹלָם כִּי אִם יְחִידֵי סְגֻלָּה בְּחִינַת יָחִיד מֻמְחֶה וּמִכָּל שֶׁכֵּן לְדַבֵּק עַצְמוֹ בְּהַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת בְּכָל דָּבָר לְהַחֲיוֹת עַצְמוֹ בִּבְחִינַת הַחִיּוּת אֱלֹקוּת שֶׁהוּא מְחַיֶּה וּמְקַיֵּם הָעוֹלָם קֹדֶם מַתַּן תּוֹרָה זֶה בְּוַדַּאי לָאו כָּל אָדָם זוֹכֶה כִּי הוּא בְּחִינָה גָּבֹהַּ מְאֹד לִמְצֹא וּלְגַלּוֹת אֱלֹקוּתוֹ יִתְבָּרַךְ, כִּבְיָכוֹל, הַנֶּעְלָם בְּכָל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם.</div>

<p>For in truth, a simple man of lesser stature — that is, the common masses — certainly does not sustain the world through the Torah, for they are not Torah scholars. And even one who does engage in Torah — not everyone merits that he sustain the entire world, but only rare, select individuals, in the aspect of <em>yachid mumcheh</em> <span class="added">[singular expert]</span>. And all the more so to attach oneself to the concealed Torah in every thing, to sustain oneself through the aspect of the divine life-force that sustains and upholds the world before the giving of the Torah — this certainly not every person merits, for it is a very lofty aspect: to find and reveal His G-dliness, blessed be He, as it were, concealed in every thing in the world.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְעַל-כֵּן כָּל הַפְּשׁוּטִים, דְּהַיְנוּ הֲמוֹן עַם צְרִיכִין לְקַבֵּל הַחִיּוּת מֵאִישׁ פָּשׁוּט הַגָּדוֹל, דְּהַיְנוּ הַצַּדִּיק הַגָּדוֹל מְאֹד שֶׁהוּא לִפְעָמִים אִישׁ פָּשׁוּט וּמִתְבַּטֵּל מֵהַתּוֹרָה וְאָז הוּא מְחַיֶּה עַצְמוֹ מֵהַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת וְעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה הוּא מְחַיֶּה כָּל הַפְּשׁוּטִים, כַּמְבֹאָר שָׁם הֵיטֵב בַּמַּאֲמָר הַנַּ״ל, עַיֵּן שָׁם.</div>

<p>Therefore, all the simple people — that is, the common masses — need to receive their life-force from the great simple man — that is, the very great <em>tzadik</em>, who is at times a simple man and ceases from the Torah, and then he sustains himself from the concealed Torah — and through this he sustains all the simple people, as is explained there well in the aforementioned discourse; see there.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְעַל-כֵּן עִקַּר כֹּחַ הַנֶּדֶר וּשְׁבוּעָה שֶׁיּוּכַל הָאָדָם לַעֲשׂוֹת תּוֹרָה מִכָּל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם עַל-יְדֵי נֶדֶר וּשְׁבוּעָה זֶה תָּלוּי רַק בִּגְדוֹלֵי הַדּוֹר שֶׁהֵם מְחַיִּין עַצְמָן בְּעֵת פְּשִׁיטוּתָן בִּשְׁעַת בִּטּוּל תּוֹרָה מֵהַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת כַּנַּ״ל, וּמִכָּל שֶׁכֵּן בְּעֵת עוֹסְקָם בַּתּוֹרָה שֶׁאָז הֵם מְחַיִּין כָּל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם עַל-יְדֵי תּוֹרָתָן וּמֵאֵלּוּ הַגְּדוֹלֵי הַדּוֹר מְקַבְּלִים חִיּוּת גַּם כָּל הֶהָמוֹן וּמֵהֶם נִשְׁתַּלְשֵׁל הַכֹּחַ גַּם לַהֲמוֹן עַם שֶׁיִּהְיֶה לָהֶם כֹּחַ לַעֲשׂוֹת תּוֹרָה מִכָּל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם עַל-יְדֵי נֶדֶר וּשְׁבוּעָה, כִּי עִקַּר זֶה הַכֹּחַ לַעֲשׂוֹת תּוֹרָה מִכָּל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם, שֶׁזֶּהוּ בְּחִינַת נֶדֶר וּשְׁבוּעָה, זֶה נִמְשָׁךְ רַק מִגְּדוֹלֵי הַדּוֹר כַּנַּ״ל:</div>

<p>Therefore, the primary power of <em>neder</em> and <em>shevuah</em> — that a person can make Torah from any thing in the world through a vow and an oath — this depends only on the great ones of the generation, who sustain themselves during their time of simplicity, at the time of cessation of Torah, from the concealed Torah, as mentioned above. And all the more so at the time of their engagement in the Torah, when they sustain all things in the world through their Torah. And from these great ones of the generation, all the masses also receive life-force, and from them the power cascades down also to the common masses — that they should have the power to make Torah from any thing in the world through a vow and an oath. For the primary power to make Torah from every thing in the world, which is the aspect of <em>neder</em> and <em>shevuah</em>, is drawn only from the great ones of the generation, as mentioned above.</p>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה שֶׁהִתְחִילָה הַתּוֹרָה פָּרָשַׁת נְדָרִים, וַיְדַבֵּר מֹשֶׁה אֶל רָאשֵׁי הַמַּטּוֹת וְכוּ'. מַה שֶּׁלֹּא נֶאֱמַר כֵּן בִּשְׁאָר מִצְוֹת הַתּוֹרָה רַק בְּכָאן אֵצֶל נְדָרִים נֶאֱמַר רָאשֵׁי הַמַּטּוֹת, 'רָאשֵׁי הַמַּטּוֹת' דַּיְקָא. כִּי עִקַּר מִצְוָה זוֹ שֶׁל נְדָרִים וּשְׁבוּעוֹת הוּא תָּלוּי בְּרָאשֵׁי הַמַּטּוֹת שֶׁהֵם גְּדוֹלֵי הַדּוֹר כַּנַּ״ל. וְעַל-כֵּן לָמְדוּ רַבּוֹתֵינוּ זַ״ל מִזֶּה שֶׁהֶחָכָם עוֹקֵר הַנֶּדֶר מֵעִקָּרוֹ, כִּי מֵאַחַר שֶׁעִקַּר הַנֶּדֶר הוּא נִמְשָׁךְ מֵחֲכַם הַדּוֹר, עַל-כֵּן בְּוַדַּאי יֵשׁ כֹּחַ בְּיָדוֹ לְהַתִּירוֹ וּלְעָקְרוֹ מֵאַחַר שֶׁכָּל עִקַּר כֹּחַ הַנֶּדֶר נִמְשָׁךְ מִמֶּנּוּ כַּנַּ״ל:</div>

<p>And this is the reason the Torah introduced <em>parshas</em> Nedarim <span class="added">[with the words]</span>: <span class="verse">"And Moshe spoke to the heads of the tribes…" <span class="verse-source">(Numbers 30:2)</span></span> which is not said regarding the other <em>mitzvos</em> of the Torah. Only here, by <em>nedarim</em>, is it said <strong>"the heads of the tribes"</strong> — "the heads of the tribes" specifically. For this <em>mitzvah</em> of <em>nedarim</em> and <em>shevuos</em> is primarily dependent on the heads of the tribes, who are the great ones of the generation, as mentioned above. And therefore our Sages of blessed memory derived from this that <strong>the <em>chacham</em> uproots the <em>neder</em> from its root</strong> — for since the root of the <em>neder</em> is drawn from the <em>chacham</em> of the generation, therefore he certainly has the power to annul it and uproot it, since the entire root of the power of the <em>neder</em> is drawn from him, as mentioned above.</p>
