<span class="section-num">9.</span>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew § 9</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה בְּחִינַת אִסּוּר נִדָּה וְטָהֳרַת הַמִּקְוֶה וּבְחִינַת תְּשׁוּבָה. כִּי דַּם נִדּוּת זֶה בְּחִינַת זֻהֲמַת הַנָּחָשׁ, כִּי עַל-יְדֵי חֵטְא אָדָם הָרִאשׁוֹן שֶׁעַל יָדוֹ נִמְשַׁךְ זֻהֲמַת הַנָּחָשׁ, עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה נַעֲשֶׂה דַּם נִדּוּת, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, הַרְבָּה אַרְבֶּה עִצְּבוֹנֵךְ. וְדָרְשׁוּ רַבּוֹתֵינוּ זַ"ל, זֶה דַּם נִדּוּת. וְעִקַּר הַעֲלָמַת הָאוֹר הַגָּנוּז שֶׁנֶּעְלַם וְנִגְנַז הָאוֹר הַגָּנוּז שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת שֶׁהִיא מְחַיָּה כָּל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם, עִקַּר הַהַעֲלָמָה וְהַהַסְתָּרָה הוּא מֵחֲמַת זֻהֲמַת הַנָּחָשׁ בְּחִינַת דַּם נִדּוּת. כִּי קֹדֶם חֵטְא אָדָם הָרִאשׁוֹן אָז הָיָה הָעוֹלָם זַךְ וְטָהוֹר וְאָז הָיְתָה הַשָּגַת אָדָם הָרִאשׁוֹן מְאִירָה מְאֹד מְאֹד וְאָז הָיוּ יְכוֹלִים לְהִסְתַּכֵּל בְּכָל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם וְלִרְאוֹת בּוֹ הַחִיּוּת אֱלֹקוּת, כִּבְיָכוֹל, הַמְחַיֶּה אוֹתוֹ. וְזֶה בְּחִינַת אוֹר שֶׁל שִׁבְעַת יְמֵי בְּרֵאשִׁית שֶׁהָיָה אָדָם מִסְתַּכֵּל בּוֹ מִסּוֹף הָעוֹלָם וְעַד סוֹפוֹ. הַיְנוּ שֶׁבָּאוֹר הַזֶּה הָיוּ יְכוֹלִים לְהַבִּיט וּלְהִסְתַּכֵּל בְּכָל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם הַגַּשְׁמִי וְלִרְאוֹת בּוֹ הַחִיּוּת אֱלֹקוּת, כִּבְיָכוֹל, הַנֶּעְלָם בּוֹ שֶׁהוּא מְחַיֶּה אוֹתוֹ הַדָּבָר. וְזֶה בְּחִינַת מִסּוֹף הָעוֹלָם וְעַד סוֹפוֹ מִקָּצֶה וְעַד קָצֶה, הַיְנוּ מִסּוֹף נְקֻדַּת הַמֶּרְכָּז שֶׁל הָעוֹלָם הַגַּשְׁמִי עַד סוֹפוֹ הָעֶלְיוֹן. שֶׁשָּׁם הַדָּבָר נִכְלָל בְּשָׁרְשׁוֹ, כִּי הַתְחָלַת הַדָּבָר בְּשָׁרְשׁוֹ הָעֶלְיוֹן הוּא בְּחִינַת סוֹף מִמַּטָּה לְמַעְלָה, הַיְנוּ שֶׁהָיָה יָכֹל לְהִסְתַּכֵּל בְּכָל הָעוֹלָם וְלִרְאוֹת בּוֹ סוֹפוֹ הָעֶלְיוֹן, שֶׁהוּא מְקֻשָּׁר לְשָׁרְשׁוֹ, הַיְנוּ שֶׁהָיָה יָכֹל לִרְאוֹת הַחִיּוּת אֱלֹקוּת, כִּבְיָכוֹל, הַנֶּעְלָם בְּכָל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם. וְאָז הָיוּ יְכוֹלִים לֵידַע הַתּוֹרָה שֶׁבְּכָל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם. אֲבָל עַל-יְדֵי חֵטְא אָדָם הָרִאשׁוֹן נִגְנַז הָאוֹר הַזֶּה, כְּמוֹ שֶׁאָמְרוּ רַבּוֹתֵינוּ זַ"ל, רָאָה שֶׁאֵין הָעוֹלָם כְּדַאי עָמַד וּגְנָזוֹ וְכוּ'. כִּי מֵחֲמַת חֵטְא אָדָם הָרִאשׁוֹן שֶׁנִּמְשָׁךְ עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה זֻהֲמַת הַנָּחָשׁ בָּעוֹלָם, בְּחִינַת דַּם נִדּוּת, עַל-כֵּן הֻצְרַךְ, כִּבְיָכוֹל, לִגְנֹז הָאוֹר כְּדֵי, שֶׁלֹּא יִינְקוּ הַקְּלִפּוֹת חַס וְשָׁלוֹם, יוֹתֵר מִדַּאי וְעִקָּר הוּא מֵחֲמַת בְּחִינַת דַּם נִדּוּת, כִּי יֵשׁ עֲשָׂרָה מִינֵי דָּמִים וִינִיקָתָם מִבְּחִינַת הַעֲלָמַת וְהַסְתָּרַת הָעֲשֶׂרֶת הַדִּבְּרוֹת, שֶׁהֵם בְּחִינַת חָמֵשׁ כְּנֶגֶד חָמֵשׁ. שֶׁמִּשָּׁם מֵהַעֲלָמָה וְהַסְתָּרָה זוֹ מִשְׁתַּלְשֵׁל וְיוֹרֵד יְנִיקָה לִבְחִינַת עֲשָׂרָה מִינֵי דָּמִים, שֶׁהֵם בְּחִינַת חֲמִשָּׁה מִינֵי דָּמִים טְמֵאִים וַחֲמִשָּׁה מִינִים טְהוֹרִים וְכַמּוּבָא. וּמֵחֲמַת, שֶׁנִּמְשָׁךְ יְנִיקָה עַל-יְדֵי חֵטְא אָדָם הָרִאשׁוֹן לִבְחִינַת עֲשָׂרָה מִינֵי דָּמִים, שֶׁיְּנִיקָתָם מִבְּחִינָה הַנַּ"ל, עַל-כֵּן הֻכְרַח הָאוֹר שֶׁל הָעֲשֶׂרֶת הַדִּבְּרוֹת לִגָּנֵז וּלְהֵעָלֵם כְּדֵי שֶׁלֹּא יִהְיֶה לָהֶם יְנִיקָה חַס וְשָׁלוֹם, יוֹתֵר מִדַּאי וְעַל-כֵּן לֹא הָיוּ יְכוֹלִים יִשְׂרָאֵל לְקַבֵּל אֶת הַתּוֹרָה עַד שֶׁסָּפְרוּ שִׁבְעָה שָׁבוּעוֹת בְּחִינַת שִׁבְעָה נְקִיִּים לְטַהֵר עַצְמָן מִדַּם נִדּוּת כִּי עִקַּר קַבָּלַת הַתּוֹרָה הוּא לְגַלּוֹת הַהַעֲלָמָה. וּכְמוֹ שֶׁאִיתָא בַּזֹּהַר הַקָּדוֹשׁ , מַאי תּוֹרָה דְּאוֹרֵי וְגָלֵי בַּמֶּה דַּהֲוֵי סְתִים וְכַנַּ"ל. וְהִתְגַּלּוּת הָאוֹר הַנֶּעְלָם אִי אֶפְשָׁר כִּי אִם כְּשֶׁמְּטַהֲרִין עַצְמָן מִדַּם נִדּוּת. כִּי כָּל זְמַן שֶׁיֵּשׁ בְּחִינַת דַּם נִדּוּת מֻכְרָח הָאוֹר לְהִתְעַלֵּם כַּנַּ"ל. וְעַל-כֵּן הֵם שִׁבְעָה נְקִיִּים כְּנֶגֶד שֶׁבַע מִדּוֹת בְּחִינַת שִׁבְעַת יְמֵי הַבִּנְיָן, כִּי עִקַּר אֲחִיזַת הַדַּם נִדּוּת, הַיְנוּ בְּחִינַת הַקְּלִפּוֹת הוּא רַק בִּבְחִינַת שִׁבְעַת יְמֵי הַבִּנְיָן שֶׁשָּׁם עִקַּר הִתְגַּלּוּת הַתּוֹרָה, כִּי עִקַּר הִתְגַּלּוּת הַתּוֹרָה הוּא עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁבַע מִדּוֹת כַּיָּדוּעַ, כִּי לְמַעְלָה מֵהַמִּדּוֹת זֶה בְּחִינַת אוֹר הַגָּנוּז שֶׁאֵין יְכוֹלִין לְהַשִּיגוֹ עַכְשָׁו. וְעַל-כֵּן כָּל זְמַן שֶׁיֵּשׁ בְּחִינַת דַּם נִדּוּת אֵין הַתּוֹרָה יְכוֹלָה לְהִתְגַּלּוֹת בִּבְחִינַת הַשֶּׁבַע מִדּוֹת כְּדֵי שֶׁלֹּא יִהְיוּ לָהֶם יְנִיקָה חַס וְשָׁלוֹם יוֹתֵר מִדַּאי, כִּי שָׁם עִקַּר אֲחִיזָתָם כַּנַּ"ל. וְעַל-כֵּן מֻכְרָח שֶׁיִּהְיֶה הַתּוֹרָה בִּבְחִינַת הֶעְלֵם כִּי שָׁם בִּבְחִינַת הֶעְלֵם, שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת לְמַעְלָה מֵהַמִּדּוֹת, אֵין לָהֶם שׁוּם אֲחִיזָה כְּלָל. וְעַל-כֵּן לֹא הָיוּ יִשְׂרָאֵל יְכוֹלִים לְקַבֵּל אֶת הַתּוֹרָה עַד שֶׁסָּפְרוּ שִׁבְעָה נְקִיִּים כְּנֶגֶד שִׁבְעַת יְמֵי הַבִּנְיָן בְּחִינַת שֶׁבַע מִדּוֹת, שֶׁשָּׁם עִקַּר אֲחִיזָתָם כְּדֵי לְטַהֲרָם מִבְּחִינַת דַּם נִדּוּת, כְּדֵי שֶׁתּוּכַל הַתּוֹרָה לְהִתְגַּלּוֹת בְּתוֹךְ הָעוֹלָם, שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת כְּלָלִיּוּת שִׁבְעַת יְמֵי הַבִּנְיָן, שֶׁהֵם כְּלָלִיּוּת הָעוֹלָם, שֶׁהֵם בְּחִינַת שֶׁבַע מִדּוֹת שֶׁעִקַּר הִתְגַּלּוּת הַתּוֹרָה עַל יָדָם כַּנַּ"ל:</div>

<p class="first">And this is the aspect of the <strong>prohibition of <span class="key-term">nidah</span></strong> <span class="added">[menstrual impurity]</span> and the <strong>purification of the <span class="key-term">mikveh</span></strong>, and the aspect of <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span> <span class="added">[repentance]</span>. For <em>dam nidos</em> <span class="added">[menstrual blood]</span> — this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">zuhamas hanachash</span> <span class="added">[the contamination of the Serpent]</span>. For through the sin of Adam HaRishon, through which the contamination of the Serpent was drawn down — through this, <em>dam nidos</em> came into being, as it is written, <span class="verse-inline">"I will greatly increase your suffering"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Genesis 3:16)</span>. And our Sages of blessed memory expounded: this refers to <em>dam nidos</em>.</p>

<p>And the primary concealment of the <span class="key-term">or haganuz</span> <span class="added">[hidden light]</span> — that the hidden light was concealed and stored away, which is the aspect of the concealed Torah that gives life to all things in the world — the primary concealment and hiddenness is because of the contamination of the Serpent, the aspect of <em>dam nidos</em>. For before the sin of Adam HaRishon, the world was pure and clean, and the perception of Adam HaRishon was illuminating exceedingly, and then one could gaze at every thing in the world and see in it the divine life-force, as it were, that gives it life.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <strong>light of the seven days of creation</strong>, through which Adam could see from one end of the world to the other. That is, through this light one could gaze and look at every thing in the physical world and see in it the divine life-force, as it were, concealed within it, that gives that thing its life. And this is the aspect of "from one end of the world to its <span class="added">[other]</span> end, from one extreme to the <span class="added">[other]</span> extreme" — that is, from the end-point of the center of the physical world to its upper end, where the thing is included in its root. For the beginning of the thing in its upper root is the aspect of "end" from below to above. That is, he could gaze at the entire world and see in it its upper end — that it is connected to its root. That is, he could see the divine life-force, as it were, concealed in every thing in the world. And then they could know the Torah that is in every thing in the world.</p>

<p>But through the sin of Adam HaRishon, this light was stored away, as our Sages of blessed memory said: <span class="verse-inline">"He saw that the world was not worthy — He arose and stored it away"</span> etc. For because of the sin of Adam HaRishon, through which the contamination of the Serpent was drawn into the world, the aspect of <em>dam nidos</em> — therefore it was necessary, as it were, to store away the light, so that the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> <span class="added">[husks/forces of impurity]</span> would not draw sustenance, G-d forbid, excessively. And the essence of this is because of the aspect of <em>dam nidos</em>, for there are <strong>ten types of blood</strong>, and their sustenance derives from the aspect of the concealment and hiddenness of the Ten Commandments, which are in the aspect of five corresponding to five. And from there, from this concealment and hiddenness, sustenance cascades down to the aspect of ten types of blood — which are five types of impure blood and five types of pure blood, as is brought.</p>

<p>And because sustenance was drawn through the sin of Adam HaRishon to the aspect of the ten types of blood, whose sustenance derives from the aforementioned aspect — therefore the light of the Ten Commandments was compelled to be stored away and concealed, so that they should not have sustenance, G-d forbid, excessively. And therefore Israel could not receive the Torah until they counted <strong>seven weeks</strong>, in the aspect of <span class="key-term">shivah nekiyim</span> <span class="added">[seven clean days]</span>, to purify themselves from <em>dam nidos</em>. For the primary purpose of receiving the Torah is to reveal the concealment, as is found in the holy Zohar: <span class="verse-inline">"What is Torah? That which reveals and discloses what was hidden"</span>, as mentioned above. And the revelation of the concealed light is impossible except when one purifies oneself from <em>dam nidos</em>. For as long as there is an aspect of <em>dam nidos</em>, the light is compelled to remain concealed, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And therefore they are <strong>seven clean days</strong>, corresponding to the <strong>seven <em>midos</em></strong> <span class="added">[attributes/sefiiros]</span>, the aspect of the seven days of construction. For the primary hold of <em>dam nidos</em> — that is, the aspect of the <em>klipos</em> — is only in the aspect of the seven days of construction, where the primary revelation of the Torah takes place. For the primary revelation of the Torah is through the seven <em>midos</em>, as is known. For above the <em>midos</em>, this is the aspect of the hidden light that cannot be attained now. And therefore, as long as there is an aspect of <em>dam nidos</em>, the Torah cannot be revealed through the aspect of the seven <em>midos</em>, so that they should not have sustenance, G-d forbid, excessively — for there is where their primary hold is, as mentioned above. And therefore the Torah must remain in a state of concealment, for there, in the state of concealment — which is the aspect of above the <em>midos</em> — they have no hold at all. And therefore Israel could not receive the Torah until they counted seven clean days, corresponding to the seven days of construction, the aspect of the seven <em>midos</em>, where their primary hold is — in order to purify them from the aspect of <em>dam nidos</em>, so that the Torah could be revealed within the world, which is the aspect of the totality of the seven days of construction — which are the totality of the world — which are the aspect of the seven <em>midos</em> through which the Torah is primarily revealed, as mentioned above.</p>

