<span class="section-num">11.</span>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew § 11</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְאַחַר הַשִּׁבְעָה נְקִיִּים הִיא צְרִיכָה לְהִטָּהֵר בְּמִקְוֶה. וּמִקְוֶה הִיא בְּחִינַת בִּינָה עָלְמָא דְּאָתֵי כַּמּוּבָא, בְּחִינַת תְּשׁוּבָה. זֶה בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת הַנַּ"ל, שֶׁהֵם כְּלָלִיּוּת עֲשֶׂרֶת הַדִּבְּרוֹת הַכְּלוּלִים בְּאָנֹכִי, שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת בִּינָה כַּמּוּבָא. כִּי כְּשֶׁצְּרִיכִין לַעֲלוֹת מִטֻּמְאָה לְטָהֳרָה לִטָּהֵר מִדַּם נִדּוּת, צְרִיכִין לְדַבֵּק עַצְמוֹ בִּבְחִינַת הָאוֹר הַגָּנוּז, הַיְנוּ הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת שֶׁשָּׁם אֵין שׁוּם פְּגָם מַגִּיעַ כְּלָל וְשָׁם כֻּלּוֹ טוֹב וּכְשֶׁמְּדַבְּקִין עַצְמוֹ לְשָׁם יְכוֹלִין לָשׁוּב אֶל ה' אֲפִלּוּ מִשְּׁאוֹל תַּחְתִּיּוֹת. וְכַמְרֻמָּז שָׁם בְּדִבְרֵי רַבֵּנוּ הַנַּ"ל בְּסוֹף דְּבָרָיו שָׁם שֶׁדִּבֵּר מֵעִנְיָן זֶה שֶׁאֲפִלּוּ בַּשְּׁאוֹל תַּחְתִּיּוֹת אֵין יֵאוּשׁ בָּעוֹלָם כְּלָל, כִּי גַּם מִשָּׁם יְכוֹלִין לָשׁוּב אֶל ה'. וְזֶהוּ עַל-יְדֵי בְּחִינַת הַנֶּאֱמָר בַּמַּאֲמָר הַנַּ"ל, הַיְנוּ עַל-יְדֵי בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת שֶׁלְּשָׁם נִמְשָׁךְ חִיּוּת מִכָּל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם וְשָׁם אֵין שׁוּם פְּגָם מַגִּיעַ וְשָׁם כֻּלּוֹ טוֹב. וַאֲפִלּוּ הַטֻּמְאָה וְהַסִּטְרָא אָחֳרָא מְקַבֶּלֶת חִיּוּת מֵהַעֲלָמָה זוֹ וּכְשֶׁמְּדַבְּקִין עַצְמָן בָּאוֹר הַגָּנוּז הַזֶּה אֲזַי נִתְבַּטֵּל הַטֻּמְאָה וְהַסִּטְרָא אָחֳרָא, כִּי עִקַּר חִיּוּתָם רַק מֵהַהַעֲלָמָה וְהַהַסְתָּרָה וְכַמְבֹאָר עִנְיָן זֶה בְּמָקוֹם אַחֵר ((בְּלִקּוּטֵי תִּנְיָנָא סִימָן יב). וְהַכְּלָל, שֶׁשָּׁם בִּבְחִינַת הָאוֹר הַגָּנוּז הַזֶּה הוּא כֻּלּוֹ טוֹב וְשָׁם עוֹלִין מִטֻּמְאָה לְטָהֳרָה וְכַנַּ"ל. וְזֶה בְּחִינַת מִקְוֶה שֶׁהִיא בְּחִינַת הָאוֹר הַגָּנוּז, הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת וְכַנַּ"ל. וְזֶה בְּחִינַת מִקְוֶה שֶׁל אַרְבָּעִים סְאָה, בְּחִינַת אַרְבָּעִים יוֹם שֶׁבָּהֶם נִתְּנָה הַתּוֹרָה, הַיְנוּ שֶׁבָּהֶם נִתְגַּלָּה הַתּוֹרָה מֵהַהֶעְלֵם אֶל הַגָּלוּי, כִּי הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת הִיא בְּחִינַת בִּינָה, שֶׁהִיא בְּחִינַת אַרְבָּעִים כַּיָּדוּעַ: וְזֶה בְּחִינַת מֵימֵי הַמִּקְוֶה שֶׁהֵם בְּחִינַת מֵימֵי הַחֶסֶד, זֶה בְּחִינַת הַחֶסֶד הָעֶלְיוֹן הַנַּ"ל, בְּחִינַת חֶסֶד חִנָּם שֶׁהָיָה מְקַיֵּם הָעוֹלָם קֹדֶם מַתַּן תּוֹרָה, שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת, שֶׁעַל יָדָהּ עוֹלִין מִטֻּמְאָה לְטָהֳרָה וְכַנַּ"ל. כִּי מַיִם מְרַמְּזִים עַל בְּחִינָה זוֹ, כִּי הַמַּיִם קָדְמוּ לָעוֹלָם, כְּמוֹ שֶׁפֵּרֵשׁ רַשִׁ"י, זֶה בְּחִינַת הַחֶסֶד חִנָּם הַנַּ"ל שֶׁקָּדַם לָעוֹלָם. כִּי הַחֶסֶד חִנָּם שֶׁבּוֹ נִתְקַיֵּם הָעוֹלָם קֹדֶם מַתַּן תּוֹרָה זֶה הַחֶסֶד קָדַם לָעוֹלָם, כִּי בְּזֶה הַחֶסֶד נִבְרָא הָעוֹלָם, כִּי ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ בָּרָא אֶת הָעוֹלָם בְּחֶסֶד חִנָּם, כִּי לֹא הָיָה עֲדַיִן שׁוּם זְכוּת וְשׁוּם מַעֲשֶׂה לִבְרֹא הָעוֹלָם עַל יָדוֹ, רַק בָּרָא אֶת הָעוֹלָם בְּחֶסֶד חִנָּם בְּחִינַת עוֹלָם חֶסֶד יִבָּנֶה. וּבְזֶה הַחֶסֶד הָיָה מְקַיֵּם אֶת הָעוֹלָם כָּל זְמַן שֶׁלֹּא נִתְּנָה הַתּוֹרָה, כִּי גַּם אָז לֹא הָיָה שׁוּם זְכוּת וְכַנַּ"ל. וְזֶה בְּחִינַת הַמַּיִם קָדְמוּ לָעוֹלָם, הַיְנוּ בְּחִינַת מֵימֵי הַחֲסָדִים, בְּחִינַת חֶסֶד הַנַּ"ל שֶׁקָּדַם לָעוֹלָם, הַיְנוּ בְּחִינַת חֶסֶד חִנָּם וְכַנַּ"ל. וְזֶה בְּחִינַת מֵימֵי הַמִּקְוֶה, בְּחִינַת הַמַּיִם שֶׁקָּדְמוּ לָעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר עֲלֵיהֶם נֶאֱמַר יִקָּווּ הַמַּיִם מִתַּחַת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְכוּ', שֶׁזֶּה בְּחִינַת מִקְוֶה אֲשֶׁר עַל-יְדֵי הַמַּיִם הַלָּלוּ, בְּחִינַת חֶסֶד חִנָּם הַנַּ"ל, שֶׁהִיא בְּחִינַת הַתּוֹרָה הַנֶּעְלֶמֶת כַּנַּ"ל, עַל יָדָם עוֹלִין מִטֻּמְאָה לְטָהֳרָה, שֶׁזֶּהוּ בְּחִינַת תְּשׁוּבָה, בְּחִינַת נֶדֶר, בְּחִינַת יוֹם הַכִּפּוּרִים שֶׁאוֹמְרִים כָּל נִדְרֵי. כִּי נֶדֶר וּמִקְוֶה וּתְשׁוּבָה וְיוֹם הַכִּפּוּרִים הַכֹּל בְּחִינָה אַחַת, בְּחִינַת עָלְמָא דְּאָתֵי שֶׁאָז יִתְגַּלֶּה הָאוֹר הַגָּנוּז שֶׁל שִׁבְעַת יְמֵי בְּרֵאשִׁית. וְאָז יִתְגַּלֶּה אֱלֹקוּתוֹ, שֶׁהָיָה נֶעְלָם בְּכָל דָּבָר שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם וְאָז יַשִּיגוּ אֱלֹקוּתוֹ יִתְבָּרַךְ מִכָּל הַדְּבָרִים שֶׁבָּעוֹלָם. וְיֵדַע כָּל פָּעוּל כִּי אַתָּה פְּעַלְתּוֹ וְיָבִין כָּל יְצוּר כִּי אַתָּה יְצַרְתּוֹ וְכוּ'. וְאָז יִתְבַּטֵּל הַסִּטְרָא אָחֳרָא עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה מֵאַחַר שֶׁיִּתְגַּלֶּה אֱלֹקוּתוֹ יִתְבָּרַךְ, כִּי הוּא יִתְבָּרַךְ מְחַיֶּה אֶת כֻּלָּם. וְאָז יִתְקַיֵּם, וְאֶת רוּחַ הַטֻּמְאָה אַעֲבִיר מִן הָאָרֶץ. וְאָז יִתְתַּקֵּן הַכֹּל וְכַנַּ"ל בָּרוּךְ ה' לְעוֹלָם, אָמֵן וְאָמֵן:</div>

<p class="first">And after the seven clean days she must purify herself in a <strong>mikveh</strong>. And the mikveh is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Binah</span>, <span class="key-term">alma d'asay</span> <span class="added">[the World to Come]</span>, as is brought — the aspect of <em>teshuvah</em>. This is the aspect of the aforementioned concealed Torah, which is the totality of the Ten Commandments comprised within <span class="verse-inline">"Anochi"</span> <span class="added">["I am" — the first of the Ten Commandments]</span>, which is the aspect of Binah, as is brought.</p>

<p>For when one needs to ascend from impurity to purity, to purify oneself from <em>dam nidos</em>, one must attach oneself to the aspect of the <em>or haganuz</em> <span class="added">[hidden light]</span> — that is, the concealed Torah — where no blemish reaches at all, and there it is entirely good. And when one attaches oneself there, one can return to Hashem even from the lowest depths. As is alluded to there in the words of our Rebbe, at the end of his words there, where he spoke about this matter — that even in the lowest depths <strong>there is no despair in the world at all</strong>, for even from there one can return to Hashem. And this is through the aspect spoken of in the aforementioned discourse — that is, through the aspect of the concealed Torah, to which life-force is drawn from all things in the world, and there no blemish reaches, and there it is entirely good.</p>

<p>And even the impurity and the <em>Sitra Achara</em> <span class="added">[the Other Side]</span> receive their life-force from this concealment. And when one attaches oneself to this hidden light, then the impurity and the <em>Sitra Achara</em> are nullified — for their entire life-force is only from the concealment and hiddenness, as this matter is explained elsewhere (in Likutay Moharan II, Torah 12). And the principle is that there, in the aspect of this hidden light, it is entirely good, and there one ascends from impurity to purity, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <strong>mikveh</strong>, which is the aspect of the hidden light, the concealed Torah, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of a mikveh of <strong>forty <em>se'ah</em></strong>, the aspect of the <strong>forty days</strong> in which the Torah was given — that is, in which the Torah was revealed from concealment to revelation. For the concealed Torah is the aspect of Binah, which is the aspect of forty, as is known.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <strong>waters of the mikveh</strong>, which are the aspect of the waters of <em>chesed</em> <span class="added">[kindness]</span>. This is the aspect of the aforementioned supernal <em>chesed</em>, the aspect of <em>chesed chinam</em> that was sustaining the world before the giving of the Torah — which is the aspect of the concealed Torah, through which one ascends from impurity to purity, as mentioned above. For water alludes to this aspect, for <strong>the waters preceded the world</strong>, as Rashi explained. This is the aspect of the aforementioned <em>chesed chinam</em> that preceded the world. For the <em>chesed chinam</em> through which the world was sustained before the giving of the Torah — this <em>chesed</em> preceded the world, for through this <em>chesed</em> the world was created. For Hashem created the world through gratuitous kindness, since there was as yet no merit and no deed through which to create the world — rather, He created the world through <em>chesed chinam</em>, in the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">"the world is built on <em>chesed</em>"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Psalms 89:3)</span>. And through this <em>chesed</em> He was sustaining the world as long as the Torah had not been given, for also then there was no merit, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of "the waters preceded the world" — that is, the aspect of the waters of <em>chasadim</em> <span class="added">[kindnesses]</span>, the aspect of the aforementioned <em>chesed</em> that preceded the world — that is, the aspect of <em>chesed chinam</em>, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of the waters of the mikveh, the aspect of the waters that preceded the world, concerning which it is said, <span class="verse-inline">"Let the waters be gathered from beneath the heavens"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Genesis 1:9)</span> etc. — and this is the aspect of <em>mikveh</em> <span class="added">[literally: "gathering"]</span>. For through these waters — the aspect of the aforementioned <em>chesed chinam</em>, which is the aspect of the concealed Torah, as mentioned above — through them one ascends from impurity to purity.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <strong><em>teshuvah</em></strong>, the aspect of a <strong><em>neder</em></strong>, the aspect of <strong>Yom HaKipurim</strong> <span class="added">[the Day of Atonement]</span> when we say <span class="key-term">Kol Nidray</span> <span class="added">[All Vows]</span>. For <em>neder</em>, mikveh, <em>teshuvah</em>, and Yom HaKipurim are all one aspect — the aspect of <em>alma d'asay</em> <span class="added">[the World to Come]</span>, when the hidden light of the seven days of creation will be revealed. And then His G-dliness that was concealed in every thing in the world will be revealed, and then they will perceive His G-dliness, blessed be He, from all things in the world: <span class="verse-inline">"And every creature shall know that You created it, and every being shall understand that You formed it"</span> etc. And then the <em>Sitra Achara</em> will be nullified through this, since His G-dliness, blessed be He, will be revealed — for He, blessed be He, gives life to all of them. And then shall be fulfilled: <span class="verse-inline">"And the spirit of impurity I will remove from the earth"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Zechariah 13:2)</span>. And then everything will be rectified, as mentioned above. Blessed be Hashem forever, <em>Amen</em> and <em>Amen</em>.</p>

